  "findings": [
    "The same staged policy, map seed, and explicit action_random_seed produced byte-identical stochastic evaluation reports across two runs.",
    "The seeded stochastic trace survived to 180.0095s with normalized action entropy 0.8275 and no low-health risk in the sampled windows.",
    "At the 60s handoff, the player was in open space around (497.8561, 133.6539), not pinned at the deterministic failure corner (-1200, -900).",
    "The 60-75s handoff bucket sampled actions 0/1/2/3/4/5/6/7/8 instead of deterministic action 7 only, keeping boundary and enemy pressure low.",
    "This is reproducible diagnostic evidence that action sampling can avoid the argmax wall-pushing handoff, not policy acceptance or stage03 permission."
